{
  "number": 11,
  "chapter": "Romans 11",
  "source": "https://berean.bible/downloads.htm",
  "translation": "Berean Standard Bible (BSB)",
  "verses": [
    {
      "verse": 1,
      "text": "I ask then, did God reject His people? Certainly not! I am an Israelite myself, a descendant of Abraham, from the tribe of Benjamin."
    },
    {
      "verse": 2,
      "text": "God did not reject His people, whom He foreknew. Do you not know what the Scripture says about Elijah, how he appealed to God against Israel:"
    },
    {
      "verse": 3,
      "text": "“Lord, they have killed Your prophets and torn down Your altars. I am the only one left, and they are seeking my life as well”?"
    },
    {
      "verse": 4,
      "text": "And what was the divine reply to him? “I have reserved for Myself seven thousand men who have not bowed the knee to Baal.”"
    },
    {
      "verse": 5,
      "text": "In the same way, at the present time there is a remnant chosen by grace."
    },
    {
      "verse": 6,
      "text": "And if it is by grace, then it is no longer by works. Otherwise, grace would no longer be grace."
    },
    {
      "verse": 7,
      "text": "What then? What Israel was seeking, it failed to obtain, but the elect did. The others were hardened,"
    },
    {
      "verse": 8,
      "text": "as it is written: “God gave them a spirit of stupor, eyes that could not see, and ears that could not hear, to this very day.”"
    },
    {
      "verse": 9,
      "text": "And David says: “May their table become a snare and a trap, a stumbling block and a retribution to them."
    },
    {
      "verse": 10,
      "text": "May their eyes be darkened so they cannot see, and their backs be bent forever.”"
    },
    {
      "verse": 11,
      "text": "I ask then, did they stumble so as to fall beyond recovery? Certainly not! However, because of their trespass, salvation has come to the Gentiles to make Israel jealous."
    },
    {
      "verse": 12,
      "text": "But if their trespass means riches for the world, and their failure means riches for the Gentiles, how much greater riches will their fullness bring!"
    },
    {
      "verse": 13,
      "text": "I am speaking to you Gentiles. Inasmuch as I am the apostle to the Gentiles, I magnify my ministry"
    },
    {
      "verse": 14,
      "text": "in the hope that I may provoke my own people to jealousy and save some of them."
    },
    {
      "verse": 15,
      "text": "For if their rejection is the reconciliation of the world, what will their acceptance be but life from the dead?"
    },
    {
      "verse": 16,
      "text": "If the first part of the dough is holy, so is the whole batch; if the root is holy, so are the branches."
    },
    {
      "verse": 17,
      "text": "Now if some branches have been broken off, and you, a wild olive shoot, have been grafted in among the others to share in the nourishment of the olive root,"
    },
    {
      "verse": 18,
      "text": "do not boast over those branches. If you do, remember this: You do not support the root, but the root supports you."
    },
    {
      "verse": 19,
      "text": "You will say then, “Branches were broken off so that I could be grafted in.”"
    },
    {
      "verse": 20,
      "text": "That is correct: They were broken off because of unbelief, but you stand by faith. Do not be arrogant, but be afraid."
    },
    {
      "verse": 21,
      "text": "For if God did not spare the natural branches, He will certainly not spare you either."
    },
    {
      "verse": 22,
      "text": "Take notice, therefore, of the kindness and severity of God: severity to those who fell, but kindness to you, if you continue in His kindness. Otherwise you also will be cut off."
    },
    {
      "verse": 23,
      "text": "And if they do not persist in unbelief, they will be grafted in, for God is able to graft them in again."
    },
    {
      "verse": 24,
      "text": "For if you were cut from a wild olive tree, and contrary to nature were grafted into one that is cultivated, how much more readily will these, the natural branches, be grafted into their own olive tree!"
    },
    {
      "verse": 25,
      "text": "I do not want you to be ignorant of this mystery, brothers, so that you will not be conceited: A hardening in part has come to Israel, until the full number of the Gentiles has come in."
    },
    {
      "verse": 26,
      "text": "And so all Israel will be saved, as it is written: “The Deliverer will come from Zion; He will remove godlessness from Jacob."
    },
    {
      "verse": 27,
      "text": "And this is My covenant with them when I take away their sins.”"
    },
    {
      "verse": 28,
      "text": "Regarding the gospel, they are enemies on your account; but regarding election, they are loved on account of the patriarchs."
    },
    {
      "verse": 29,
      "text": "For God’s gifts and His call are irrevocable."
    },
    {
      "verse": 30,
      "text": "Just as you who formerly disobeyed God have now received mercy through their disobedience,"
    },
    {
      "verse": 31,
      "text": "so they too have now disobeyed, in order that they too may now receive mercy through the mercy shown to you."
    },
    {
      "verse": 32,
      "text": "For God has consigned everyone to disobedience so that He may have mercy on everyone."
    },
    {
      "verse": 33,
      "text": "O, the depth of the riches of the wisdom and knowledge of God! How unsearchable are His judgments, and untraceable His ways!"
    },
    {
      "verse": 34,
      "text": "“Who has known the mind of the Lord? Or who has been His counselor?”"
    },
    {
      "verse": 35,
      "text": "“Who has first given to God, that God should repay him?”"
    },
    {
      "verse": 36,
      "text": "For from Him and through Him and to Him are all things. To Him be the glory forever! Amen."
    }
  ],
